    },
    "CaseUnderstandingProvenance": {
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "description": "SLICE-3A: `CaseUnderstandingProvenanceV1` — how the sibling `case_understanding` was produced.\n\nDeliberately a SEPARATE, small envelope rather than fields inside\n`CaseUnderstandingProjection`: the projection is Brain 1's semantic content, this is metadata\nabout the run that produced it. Keeping them apart means a reader can trust the content\nwithout having to strip bookkeeping out of it, and there is still exactly one semantic\nrepresentation of the case — no third model.\n\nEvery field is optional with an honest empty default. An empty string means \"not known\",\nnever a fabricated status: a snapshot written before this slice simply has\n`case_understanding_provenance = None` and gets no invented provenance.\n\n`corrected` is NOT `degraded`. A normalisation may be a harmless synonym rewrite or a real\ndictionary collision, and nothing in the current code distinguishes them. Until a severity\ncontract exists, this records WHAT happened and refuses to editorialise about how bad it was.",
      "properties": {
        "schema_version": {
          "default": "v1",
          "title": "Schema Version",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "availability": {
          "default": "",
          "enum": [
            "available",
            "unavailable",
            "not_required",
            ""
          ],
          "title": "Availability",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "source_mode": {
          "default": "",
          "enum": [
            "model_result",
            "normalized_model_result",
            "fallback",
            "skipped_for_lane",
            ""
          ],
          "title": "Source Mode",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "validation_state": {
          "default": "",
          "enum": [
            "clean",
            "corrected",
            ""
          ],
          "title": "Validation State",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "source_signal_id": {
          "default": "",
          "title": "Source Signal Id",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "observed_at": {
          "default": "",
          "title": "Observed At",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "reason_codes": {
          "items": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "title": "Reason Codes",
          "type": "array"
        },
        "normalization_count": {
          "default": 0,
          "minimum": 0,
          "title": "Normalization Count",
          "type": "integer"
        },
        "validation_error_count": {
          "default": 0,
          "minimum": 0,
          "title": "Validation Error Count",
          "type": "integer"
        }
      },
      "title": "CaseUnderstandingProvenance",
      "type": "object"
    },
    "CaseUnderstandingStatusV1": {
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "description": "SLICE-2C: how good our reasoning about this case currently is — status ONLY.\n\n`case_understanding_provenance` records the mechanics of the run that produced the\nUnderstanding (source mode, validation state, counts). This is the one-word operator-facing\nread derived from it, so consumers stop re-deriving \"is our understanding good enough?\" from\nprovenance internals, each with its own rules.\n\nHard boundary, and the reason this slice exists: **this field must never influence feed\nmembership**. `feed_visibility` does not import or read it, and a `degraded` or `unavailable`\nstatus neither hides an existing card nor creates a new one. Understanding quality and desk\nmembership are different questions with different owners; conflating them would let a reasoning\nfailure silently remove real operator work from the desk.\n\n`reasoning_not_required` is a normal outcome, not a defect: some lanes deliberately skip heavy\nreasoning.\n\n`corrected` provenance does NOT map to `degraded` — see `CaseUnderstandingProvenance`, which\ndeliberately refuses to editorialise about how bad a normalisation was. Only a genuine\nsubstitute (`source_mode=\"fallback\"`) is reported as `degraded`.",
      "properties": {
        "schema_version": {
          "const": "case_understanding_status.v1",
          "default": "case_understanding_status.v1",
          "title": "Schema Version",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "status": {
          "enum": [
            "ok",
            "degraded",
            "unavailable",
            "reasoning_not_required"
          ],
          "title": "Status",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "source": {
          "default": "",
          "title": "Source",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "reason": {
          "default": "",
          "title": "Reason",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "reason_codes": {
          "items": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "title": "Reason Codes",
          "type": "array"
        },
        "source_signal_id": {
          "default": "",
          "title": "Source Signal Id",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "observed_at": {
          "default": "",
          "title": "Observed At",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "age_seconds": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "type": "integer"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "default": null,
          "title": "Age Seconds"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "status"
      ],
      "title": "CaseUnderstandingStatusV1",
      "type": "object"
    },
